.TH ODFVIEW 1
.\" $Id$
.SH NAME
odfview \- export a partial spreadsheet view for a selected set of tracked row/column changes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B odfview
[\fB\-c\fR \fIchange-id\fR] ...
[\fB\-a\fR]
[\fB\-l\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR \fItable\fR]
[\fB\-o\fR \fIcsv-path\fR]
[\fB\-u\fR \fIunresolvable-csv\fR]
\fIspreadsheet.ods\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B odfview
reads the unresolved table change records (row/column insertions, deletions
and movements) stored in an OpenDocument spreadsheet and rebuilds the sheet
as it would look if only the changes selected on the command line were
applied.
.PP
A selected change is kept
.IR applied .
The empty selection therefore reconstructs the original sheet: inserted
rows/columns disappear, deleted rows/columns (including their saved old
values) come back, and movements are undone. Selecting every change
reproduces the current sheet.
.PP
A change that depends on another change (for example a movement that moves
rows created by an earlier insertion) cannot be rebuilt when the prerequisite
is not selected. The cells covered by such a change are written to the
unresolvable report instead of receiving invented coordinates; all unrelated
areas of the sheet are still exported normally.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " change-id"
Keep the tracked change with this identifier applied. May be repeated. Use
.B \-l
to discover the identifiers present in the document.
.TP
.B \-a
Select every tracked change, reproducing the current sheet.
.TP
.B \-l
List the tracked changes (identifier, kind, position and dependencies) and
exit without exporting a view.
.TP
.BI \-t " table"
Table to export, given by name or zero based index. Defaults to the first
table.
.TP
.BI \-o " csv-path"
Write the reconstructed view as CSV to this file. Defaults to standard
output.
.TP
.BI \-u " unresolvable-csv"
Write the cells that cannot be rebuilt for the selection to this CSV file.
Defaults to standard error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
odfview \-l accounts.ods
odfview \-c ctm-1 \-c ctm-2 \-o view.csv \-u broken.csv accounts.ods
odfview \-a accounts.ods
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR csv2ods (1),
.BR odflint (1)
